---
import { link } from '../utils/link';
---
<section id="work" class="alt-bg">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="section-label">Work</span>
    <h2>What I Work On</h2>
    <div class="work-rows">

      <div class="work-row">
        <h3>Azure Landing Zones</h3>
        <p>
          End-to-end ALZ Corp deployments with Terraform and Bicep. 135+ automated
          checklist validations via Azure Resource Graph. Security and compliance
          built in from day one, not bolted on. Capacity, quota, and multi-region
          planning for large estates.
        </p>
        <a class="work-row-link" href={link('work#landing-zones')}>See deployment patterns</a>
      </div>

      <div class="work-row">
        <h3>Networking &amp; Connectivity</h3>
        <p>
          Hub-and-spoke and Virtual WAN designs, routing intent, private endpoints and
          DNS, central firewall egress. Routing behavior validated up front so
          segmentation and traffic paths stay predictable.
        </p>
        <a class="work-row-link" href={link('work#networking')}>See networking patterns</a>
      </div>

      <div class="work-row">
        <h3>AI Platforms &amp; Agents</h3>
        <p>
          Microsoft Foundry and Azure OpenAI behind private networking, API Management
          as the model gateway, MCP tooling, and SRE-style agents for operations. Built
          to run inside enterprise guardrails, not as isolated demos.
        </p>
        <a class="work-row-link" href={link('work#ai')}>See AI patterns</a>
      </div>

      <div class="work-row">
        <h3>AKS &amp; Kubernetes</h3>
        <p>
          AKS Automatic clusters with ALZ Corp networking. BYO VNet, Application
          Gateway for Containers, NGINX, Istio with multiple ingress and egress patterns
          documented with full Terraform parity.
        </p>
        <a class="work-row-link" href={link('work#aks')}>See AKS patterns</a>
      </div>

      <div class="work-row">
        <h3>IaC Security</h3>
        <p>
          Terraform modules built to run inside ALZ Corp landing zones: no public IPs,
          central firewall egress, managed identity everywhere. PSRule and azqr
          integrated into CI pipelines.
        </p>
        <a class="work-row-link" href={link('work#iac-security')}>See security patterns</a>
      </div>

      <div class="work-row">
        <h3>GitHub Runners &amp; CI/CD</h3>
        <p>
          GitHub-hosted and self-hosted runners with Azure VNet integration, Container
          Apps, and ALZ Corp firewall egress. GHE.com EU data residency patterns.
        </p>
        <a class="work-row-link" href={link('work#cicd')}>See runner patterns</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
